      "text": "To determine the cost of the painting in Chinese yuan, we need to convert the given amount from Namibian dollars to US dollars first, and then convert the US dollars to Chinese yuan.\n\n1. **Convert Namibian dollars to US dollars:**\n   We know that 1 US dollar is equal to 7 Namibian dollars. Therefore, the cost of the painting in US dollars is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Cost in US dollars} = \\frac{\\text{Cost in Namibian dollars}}{7} = \\frac{105}{7} = 15 \\text{ US dollars}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Convert US dollars to Chinese yuan:**\n   We know that 1 US dollar is equal to 6 Chinese yuan. Therefore, the cost of the painting in Chinese yuan is:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Cost in Chinese yuan} = \\text{Cost in US dollars} \\times 6 = 15 \\times 6 = 90 \\text{ Chinese yuan}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the cost of the painting in Chinese yuan is \\(\\boxed{90}\\).",
